msgid "``FRAMEWORK``: top-level ``meta/services.yml`` integration keys mapped to the in-axis target entity they wire the role into (the infinito-native, group-gated service flags), distinct from the curated upstream edges;"
msgstr "``FRAMEWORK``: най-високо ниво ``meta/services.yml`` интеграционните ключове, начертани на целевата ос, те предават ролята на (флаговете за обслужване с групово управление, които са в инфинито-народни), различни от извитите ръбове нагоре по веригата;"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``False`` when the covered variant pins ``services.tor.enabled`` to a literal false, ``True`` otherwise. A reactive Jinja flag counts as capable: it is the role saying \"onion when the node is dark\". Consulting the variant matters -- roles pin the gate ``true`` in variant 0 and ``false`` in the rest, so reading only the base config claims an onion for rounds that deliberately run without one."
msgstr "``False`` когато обхванатият вариант пинове ``services.tor.enabled`` до буквален фалшив, ``True`` В противен случай. Един реактивен Джинджа флаг се брои за способен: това е ролята на поговорката \"Лук, когато възелът е тъмен\". Консултиране на вариантите -- ролите забиват вратата ``true`` във вариант 0 както и ``false`` В останалата част, така че четене само основната конфигуриране твърди лук за кръгове, които умишлено тичат без един."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``GH_TOKEN`` env var"
msgstr "``GH_TOKEN`` unit description in lists"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``GITLAB_ROOT_PASSWORD`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__, from ``GITLAB_INIT_ROOT_PASSWORD`` in ```vars/main.yml`` <./vars/main.yml>`__) belongs to GitLab’s built-in ``root`` account, not to the Keycloak ``administrator`` username the persona signs in with, and no GitLab account is provisioned for ``biber`` at all — the OmniAuth sign-in is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona and the baseline assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr "``GITLAB_ROOT_PASSWORD`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__, from ``GITLAB_INIT_ROOT_PASSWORD`` in ```vars/main.yml`` <./vars/main.yml>`__) belongs to GitLab’s built-in ``root`` account, not to the Keycloak ``administrator`` username the persona signs in with, and no GitLab account is provisioned for ``biber`` at all — the OmniAuth sign-in is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona и основните твърдения работят безусловно."

